# Everything under .foundation/ is machine state: runtime records, evidence,
# receipts, sandboxes, authority requests, attestations, logs, and the install
# manifest. Only the two files the installer manages belong in history.
#
# This is an allow-list on purpose. It used to name each machine-state directory
# instead, and every directory added since had to be remembered — `authority/`
# and `attestations/` were not, so external-review records and host attestations
# surfaced as untracked files in every consumer project that used them, and
# `install-manifest.txt` did the same in every project that ran the installer.
# Ignoring by default means a new kind of machine state is ignored the day it is
# written rather than the day someone notices it in `git status`.
*
!.gitignore
!README.md
